<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:DGN_MM:1</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>DGN_MM</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>This module transforms the information from DGN format to MiraMon. The DGN format (ISFF _ Intergraph Standard File Format) is own of the program of drawing assisted by computer Microstation, of Bentley (http://www.microstation.com), very used in the engineering and architecture fields. Currently DGN v.7 and previous are read.</ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Import from the DGN Microstation format to MiraMon"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:This module transforms the information from DGN format to MiraMon."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FITXER_DGN</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DGN file.</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This is the name of the DGN file.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-DGN</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-DGN</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>INFORME</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Report</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This stores the report of the DGN content in the text file.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>COMPRIMIR</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Compression</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The content of the DGN is purified; the marked objects are eliminated and the new end of file is located. Before doing the compression, a safety copy of the original file (with extension DG$) is done. If during the reading of the objects several errors are accumulated, automatically begins a compression of the file.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SIST_DEST</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Reference system</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This is a text chain with the cartographic reference system of reference (known by MiraMon) or a local reference syste.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
					<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FACTORK</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Transformation factor</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>It is necessary to specify the transformation factor between the selected reference system and the units (principal or secondary) of the file. It is only necessary to indicate this parameter when the application has not been able to find it automatically.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
					<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>MASTER_UNITS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Units of DGN</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>When a local reference system is indicated, it is necessary to specify which are the units of DGN file to use.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>nm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>µm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>mm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>cm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>dm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>dam</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>hm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>km</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>inch</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>ft</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>yd</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>S.M.</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>N.M.</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>píxels</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SUB_UNITS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>SUB UNITS</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Sub Units</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>nm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>µm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>mm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>cm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>dm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>dam</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>hm</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>km</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>inch</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>ft</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>yd</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>S.M.</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>N.M.</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>píxels</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>ESCALAT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Scaling factor</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Scaling factor</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
					<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DESPX</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Displacing factor</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Coordinates displacing factor X</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
					<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DESPY</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Displacing factor</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Coordinates displacing factor Y</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
					<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SELECCIO_NIVELL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Stated levels</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Values between 0 and 63. Multiple values separated by a comma are accepted (f.i. /SELECCIO_NIVELL=6,10,34). If this option is present, only the elements of the stated levels will be transformed.</ows:Abstract>
