					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SELECCIO_GRUIX</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Width index</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Values between 0 and 31. This corresponds to the width index of the elements. Multiple values separated by a comma are accepted (f.i./SELECCIO_GRUIX=1,30).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>7</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>8</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>9</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>10</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>11</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>12</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>13</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>14</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>15</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>16</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>17</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>18</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>19</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>20</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>21</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>22</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>23</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>24</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>25</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>26</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>27</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>28</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>29</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>30</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>31</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SELECCIO_ESTIL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Line style</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Values between 0 and 7. This corresponds to the identification index of line style. Multiple values separated by a comma are accepted (f.i./SELECCIO_ESTIL=1,6,5).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>7</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SELECCIO_CELLULA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Chosen cells</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the chosen cells, separated by commas. If this parameter appears, OBLIGATORILY /SELECCIO_ELEMENT must contain only "2". The rest of parameters (COLOR, GRUIX -width-, ESTIL -style-) are ignored, except NIVELL -level-. IMPORTANT NOTE: If more than one option of selection is indicated (f.i./SELECCIO_ESTIL and /SELECCIO_NIVELL, an AND operator applies between these two conditions, never an OR operator.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>1NIVELL_1FITXER</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>1 Level  1File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>he whole content of each of the DGN levels are transformed in a MiraMon layer (ARC file and/or PNT file) and so many layers as levels are generated. The names of the different files are obtained from MM_FILE with a numerical suffix, which corresponds to the number of the level (f.i. FILE_MM01, FILE_MM12, etc.). If this parameter is not indicated, the whole DGN file is transformed in only one ARC or PNT file ARC.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>BD_ESTESA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>extended Data Base</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The database associated with the graphic objects (ARC and PNT) contains widespread information (connectable, modified, blocked, solid, etc), in addition to the basic information (level, colour, width and style). If this option is not indicated it is only generated the basic database.\nHow to treat cells?</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>CEL_OBJ_PRIMITIUS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Primitive objects of the cells</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The primitive objects of the cells are transformed. The options of visualization are of the individual objects, not of the cells. If no parameter is indicated (automatically): a point is generated for each cell, and its name and other characteristics are saved in the database.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>PALETACOLOR</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Color palette</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If a file name of Microstation palette (extension TBL) is indicated, this is converted to MiraMon and the suitable graphic files are linked automatically. If this parameter is not indicated, the active DGN intern colour palette is transformed, if it exists,the file DGN.</ows:Abstract>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-TBL</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-TBL</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TAULA_SIMB_TEXT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Symbolization table</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>By default a text symbolization table is created inside the output folder. By using this parameter, you can name and place this table where you want (note that the pnt file will remain linked to the table, so this table must be accessible when the layer is open). If the file already exists, previous font codes and their symbolization will be protected, so the file only will be updated if new font codes are found (the program warns when it founds a new font code).</ows:Abstract>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-DBF</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-DBF</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>COORD_TEXT_TOPO</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>No displacement</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>No default displacement</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FITXER_MM</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>MiraMon output file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This is the name of the output Map MiraMon file (without extension).</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<LiteralOutput>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#anyURI">anyURI</ows:DataType>
				</LiteralOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>